================================================================================
KEY HARDWARE TAKEAWAYS:
1. End-to-end token generation on a 24-layer LLM on physical Tesla T4 increases
   from 61.04 tokens/sec (PyTorch Eager) to 88.96 tokens/sec (Custom Fused W4A16),
   yielding a measured 1.46x end-to-end speedup on real silicon.
2. Tail latency (p99) is reduced from 26.22 ms down to 14.62 ms (44.2% tighter).
3. torch.compile on Turing fails to outperform Eager for autoregressive decode because
   in-place KV cache mutations invalidate CUDAGraph static captures.
